# The run door (notes/coc-plan.md S2): `wap wap/extensions/theory/run/door.wap --tree <root> program.wap` reads a
# program as the elaborator's door does (elaborate/door.wap), then erases what it runs (erase.wap) and prints it as
# plain wap (lower.wap), which runs as the program does: the same output, the same exit status. The first refusal is
# printed as its one line and ends the run with a failure.
use "../elaborate/file.wap"
use "../elaborate/read.wap"
use "../environment.wap"
use "erase.wap"
use "lower.wap"

theory = Theory()
door_elaborated(theory, args)
try { print written_program(running(theory)) } catch refusal { stopped_by(refusal) }
